{
  "contract_version": "authority-v1",
  "ruling": "R2, 20 Nov 2026; addendum 22 Nov 2026",
  "representation": "Run one recorded upgrade transaction only when no enabled admin exists. Resolve original bootstrap from surviving users.id=1 and sqlite_sequence(users).seq evidence; never MIN(remaining users.id). The pinned registration flow writes no dedicated bootstrap marker. The AUTOINCREMENT row-id and sqlite_sequence entry are its durable insertion evidence. Operator recovery is only the fallback when original account is missing/disabled or this evidence is genuinely absent. Addendum 22 Nov 2026: if row 1 (users.id=1) still has the shipped default password, it is never promoted, whatever its username; the first enabled account inserted after it (lowest users.id above 1, never created_at) is promoted instead, and operator recovery applies only if there is none. A default account whose password was changed is a real account and is promoted as the original.",
  "release_note_line": "The 0.9 upgrade records a one-time promotion to Admin on gateways with no enabled admin. It promotes the original enabled bootstrap account or, if that account still has the shipped default password, the next enabled account by account number. Other accounts are not promoted; if no account qualifies, operator recovery is required.",
